  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Everything about straight lines on the \\( xy \\)-plane: gradient, length, midpoint and the equation \\( y=mx+c \\). Parallel lines share a gradient; perpendicular gradients multiply to \\( -1 \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Coordinate Geometry",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "For points \\((x_1,y_1)\\) and \\((x_2,y_2)\\): gradient \\(m=\\dfrac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\); midpoint \\(=\\!\\left(\\dfrac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\dfrac{y_1+y_2}{2}\\right)\\); distance \\(=\\!\\sqrt{(x_2-x_1)^2+(y_2-y_1)^2}\\). Two lines are <strong>parallel</strong> if they have equal gradients. Two lines are <strong>perpendicular</strong> if the product of their gradients is \\(-1\\): \\(m_1\\times m_2=-1\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Perpendicular gradient",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(m_\\perp=-\\dfrac{1}{m}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Parallel lines",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(m_1=m_2\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "General line",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(ax+by=c\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Intercepts",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Set \\(y=0\\) or \\(x=0\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 3.B — Perpendicular line",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Line \\(\\ell\\) has equation \\(y=3x-2\\). Find the equation of the line perpendicular to \\(\\ell\\) passing through \\((6,1)\\).</p><p>Perpendicular gradient: \\(m_\\perp=-\\tfrac{1}{3}\\).</p>\\[y-1=-\\tfrac{1}{3}(x-6)\\;\\Rightarrow\\;y=-\\tfrac{1}{3}x+3.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Show that the points \\(A(1,3)\\), \\(B(4,7)\\) and \\(C(7,3)\\) form an isosceles triangle.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(AB=\\sqrt{9+16}=5\\). \\(BC=\\sqrt{9+16}=5\\). \\(AC=\\sqrt{36+0}=6\\). Since \\(AB=BC\\), triangle is isosceles.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Gradient",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( m=\\dfrac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Midpoint",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\Big(\\dfrac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\,\\dfrac{y_1+y_2}{2}\\Big) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Distance",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sqrt{(x_2-x_1)^2+(y_2-y_1)^2} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Straight line",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( y=mx+c \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 3.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the equation of the line through \\( (1,2) \\) and \\( (4,11) \\).</p><p>Gradient \\( m=\\dfrac{11-2}{4-1}=3 \\). Use \\( (1,2) \\): \\( 2=3(1)+c \\Rightarrow c=-1 \\):</p>\\[ y=3x-1. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
